---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn what Kreativ Auto covers, how guides are written, and what readers should expect." enableAds={false}>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface hero-frame p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">What Kreativ Auto is here to do</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
            Kreativ Auto exists to make automotive content easier to trust, easier to scan, and more useful when someone is trying to decide what to check, what to fix, or what to buy.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-steel">
            The focus is practical ownership questions, not generic traffic bait. That means clearer explanations, relevant next steps, and a stronger bias toward helping readers make a sensible decision.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="accent-panel p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">What readers should expect</p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="soft-panel p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">Focus</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Common problems, parts worth buying, and ownership guidance that holds up in normal use.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="soft-panel p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">Bias</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Practical fitment and decision quality over hype, catalog spam, or dramatic claims.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="soft-panel p-4 sm:col-span-2">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">Audience</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Drivers who want a better ownership decision, not a vague summary that still leaves the real question unresolved.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Topics</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Three layers of automotive guidance</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="mesh-card p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Problem guides</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Start with the symptom, narrow the likely causes, and get to a better first check before spending money blindly.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="mesh-card p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Best-parts guides</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Compare parts by real use case, fitment confidence, and ownership logic instead of padded affiliate lists.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="mesh-card p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Ownership guides</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Use the flagship guides when the real question is broader than one symptom or one part.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it is written</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">The editorial standard is deliberately narrow</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Practical over exhaustive</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The goal is not to list every theoretical possibility. The goal is to help readers get to the most defensible next step faster.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Fitment-aware over generic</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Advice is better when it is kept tied to the generation, phase, trim, engine, or drivetrain split that actually changes the decision.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Useful over performative</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Kreativ Auto is not built to pretend every repair needs the most expensive part or the most dramatic diagnosis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coverage rules</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">What earns a page</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">A real ownership decision</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            A page should answer something a driver or used-car shopper can act on: whether a symptom is urgent, which part family fits the complaint, what to check before buying, or how two versions differ.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Vehicle context</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            A recommendation is kept tied to the model year, generation, trim, engine, drivetrain, and market where those details can change the answer.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Clear limits</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            No page should pretend to inspect a car remotely. Safety issues, warning lights, brake faults, coolant loss, and steering problems still need proper diagnosis when the evidence is unclear.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Maintenance over drama</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            Most useful repair advice is not dramatic. Tire condition, brake hardware, battery health, service records, and fitment checks solve more problems than worst-case guessing.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Maintenance</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">How pages are kept useful</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
        <p>
          Pages can be revised when a model receives better coverage, when a product page changes, when a correction identifies a fitment issue, or when a guide needs a clearer first check.
        </p>
        <p>
          A visible update date appears on article-style pages when the underlying recommendation, diagnostic framing, or editorial review changes materially.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Review the project and contribute</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
        <p>
          The website source, structured content, review gates, and deployment workflow are available on GitHub. Software is licensed under MIT, while original editorial material uses CC BY-SA 4.0. Photographs and Kreativ Auto brand assets retain their separate terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contributions should preserve vehicle scope, primary-source attribution, review restrictions, and image provenance.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-flex border border-ink bg-ink px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent" href="https://github.com/aolaru/kreativ-auto" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          View source code
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
